    "custom_liquid_tRmdKP": {
      "type": "custom-liquid",
      "settings": {
        "custom_liquid": "<h2>Why Choose Ameda For Your Breast Pump?</h2>\n<p>Ameda was founded by the inventor of the hospital-grade breast pump over 80 years ago, and we&rsquo;re still dedicated to supporting breastfeeding mothers with high-quality, innovative products. Here are a few reasons why Ameda is the best choice for your breast pump needs:</p>\n<h3>Hospital-Grade Quality</h3>\n<p>Ameda pumps are inspired by our award-winning hospital-grade technology, ensuring that you get the best quality for efficient and comfortable milk expression.</p>\n<h3>Customizable Comfort</h3>\n<p>Our pumps feature adjustable suction levels and multiple pumping modes, allowing you to tailor your experience to meet your comfort needs.</p>\n<h3>Trusted by Healthcare Professionals</h3>\n<p>Ameda breast pumps are trusted by healthcare providers worldwide, with a reputation for reliability and efficiency. Over 1,000 hospitals use Ameda pumps to support breastfeeding moms.</p>\n<h3>Comprehensive Support</h3>\n<p>In addition to our high-quality breast pumps, Ameda offers award-winning customer support through our ParentCare program, providing you with guidance and assistance whenever you need it.</p>\n<h3>Commitment to Safety</h3>\n<p>All Ameda products are designed with safety in mind, using BPA-free materials to ensure that your milk remains pure and healthy for your baby.</p>\n<h3>Insurance Compatibility</h3>\n<p>We work with a wide range of providers to help moms obtain their breast pumps at little to no cost, making it easier for you to access the tools you need for successful breastfeeding.</p>\n<h2>Choosing the Right Breast Pump</h2>\n<p>Selecting the right breast pump can feel overwhelming, especially for first-time mothers. It&rsquo;s important to consider factors such as how often you&rsquo;ll be using the pump, its portability, and your comfort. Hands-free breast pumps are a fantastic option for busy moms who need to pump while multitasking or have limited time. These pumps allow you to express milk without using your hands, providing complete mobility. Additionally, many insurance plans cover the cost of breast pumps, making it easier to obtain a high-quality device with minimal out-of-pocket expenses. Explore the kinds of breast pumps offered by Ameda below.&nbsp;</p>\n<h2>Types of Breast Pumps Available Through Insurance Coverage</h2>\n<p>Navigating the types of breast pumps that are available through insurance can feel overwhelming, but Ameda makes it easy by offering a variety of options that cater to different needs and lifestyles. Here&rsquo;s a breakdown of the different types of breast pumps available through insurance from Ameda:</p>\n<h3>Hands-Free Breast Pumps Through Insurance</h3>\n<p>Hands-free pumps offer the ultimate convenience for moms who are always on the move. These pumps are designed to be worn inside your bra, allowing you to go about your day with complete mobility. Ameda&rsquo;s hands-free breast pumps offer powerful suction, comfort, and discretion, making them ideal for multitasking moms.</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.ameda.com/collections/breast-pumps\">Explore Hands Free Breast Pumps</a></p>\n<h3>Wearable Breast Pumps Through Insurance</h3>\n<p>Wearable breast pumps provide freedom and flexibility to pump whenever and wherever you need to. With lightweight and compact designs, wearable pumps fit seamlessly under clothing, allowing you to express milk discreetly. Ameda's wearable breast pumps are covered by many insurance plans, ensuring moms can enjoy hands-free pumping with hospital-grade efficiency.</p>\n<p>Explore Wearable Breast Pumps</p>\n<h3>Double Breast Pumps Through Insurance</h3>\n<p>Double breast pumps allow moms to pump from both breasts simultaneously, significantly reducing pumping time. These pumps are perfect for moms who need to express milk quickly and efficiently. Ameda&rsquo;s double breast pumps provide customizable suction levels and pumping modes, making it easy to find the perfect settings for comfort and effective milk expression.</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.ameda.com/collections/breast-pumps/products/ameda-mya-joy-plus-rechargeable-quiet-and-portable-double-breast-pump\">Explore Double Breast Pumps</a></p>\n<h3>Manual Breast Pumps Through Insurance</h3>\n<p>Manual breast pumps are a great option for moms who need a simple, portable solution for occasional pumping. These pumps are lightweight, easy to use, and do not require electricity, making them convenient for travel or when on the go. Ameda&rsquo;s manual pumps are designed for comfort and ease, providing an affordable and effective way to express milk through insurance.</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.ameda.com/collections/breast-pumps/products/one-hand-manual-breast-pump-with-flexishield\">Explore Manual Breast Pumps</a></p>\n<h3>Other Breastfeeding Essentials Through Insurance</h3>\n<p>In addition to breast pumps, many breastfeeding essentials are also available through insurance to help support your breastfeeding journey. These essentials include accessories like extra breast milk storage bottles, breast pump flanges in different sizes, silicone inserts, valves, and cleaning supplies. Having the right accessories can make a significant difference in the comfort and efficiency of your pumping sessions. Ameda works with insurance companies to help you get these essential items covered, making sure you have everything you need for a successful breastfeeding experience.</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.ameda.com/collections/accessories\">Explore Breastfeeding Accessories</a></p>",
